INT. TAXIDERMY WORKSHOP - NIGHT

Glass eyes in labelled trays. A fox mid-pounce on the workbench. Moonlight on a stuffed heron.

ORLA MCKEOWN, 30s, apron, scalpel, hums over a half-finished badger. Easy. Peaceful.

DEVRIM AYDIN, 20s, courier, jacket still on, holds a padded envelope. He wanders the shelves.

DEVRIM
Creepy in here.

ORLA
It's Tuesday.

DEVRIM
Meaning?

ORLA
Tuesday's quiet.

He picks up a jar of eyes. Rattles it. Puts it back.

DEVRIM
Package for Mr. Pemberton.

ORLA
Leave it on the desk.

DEVRIM
He has to sign.

ORLA
He's upstairs.

An intercom box on the wall crackles.

PEMBERTON (V.O.)
(through the speaker, dry)
Orla. Is that the courier?

ORLA
(to the box)
He's here.

PEMBERTON (V.O.)
Send him up. Door's open.

Orla smiles at Devrim.

ORLA
Door's open.

DEVRIM
Where's the stairs?

She points with the scalpel. Behind a curtain.

Devrim goes. His footsteps on wood. A pause. A door creaks. Then nothing.

Orla keeps stitching. The badger's fur parts under her thumb.

PEMBERTON (V.O.) (CONT'D)
(through the speaker, much closer)
Orla. Who's the boy?

She stops. The thread hangs from her needle.

ORLA
What do you mean?

PEMBERTON (V.O.)
I'm standing in the shop. Behind you.

Orla does not turn. She sets down the scalpel. Very, very slowly.

On the speaker, upstairs, a muffled thump. Footsteps run overhead.
